  "notes": "The Vushtrri Stone Bridge spans a dry meadow in nine varied pointed masonry arches. A shallow deck hump and bent centerline follow the crossing, with warm voussoir rings, a rounded stone belt, irregular upright parapet blocks and graded stone approaches. The PMTiles path fixes the approaches and heading. Arch stations, deck width and masonry courses are approximated from the exterior views. The source terrain is coarse and leaves the historic channel dry. The bridge ends blend into its unedited surface. The photos establish the profile and materials. The span distribution and parapets are visual approximations.",
